<Slide style={{
    width: 1280,
    height: 720,
    background: '#FFFFFF',
    padding: '60px 60px',
    flexDirection: 'column',
    fontFamily: '"Arial", "Microsoft YaHei", sans-serif',
}}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#3D7BD9', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 1.6 }}>
        MODEL SIDE · RQ1
    </Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 34, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#0E3F8C', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 10 }}>
        What the models get wrong instead
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ height: 1, background: '#D6DCE5', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Box style={{ flex: 1, justifyContent: 'center', alignItems: 'center' }}>
        <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', width: 1160 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, color: '#4A5568' }}>
                Reliability by outcome class — the dashed diagonal is perfect calibration.
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8B97A8' }}>local smoothing · ESS ≥ 20</Text>
        </Box>

        <Image src="assets/fig05.png" style={{ width: 1040, height: 321, marginTop: 8 }} />

        <Box style={{ width: 1160, padding: '12px 20px', background: '#F0F5FC', borderRadius: 6, marginTop: 12 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.5 }}>
                Draw is over-dispersed — slope 0.528 / 0.566 on the two boosted arms, 0.944 on B4 — while
                their home and away slopes are 1.08–1.11, i.e. under-dispersed. The market sits at
                1.06–1.09 on all three. Capacity distorts the classes in opposite directions, and ECE
                moved the other way, so the slope is our only verdict statistic.
            </Text>
        </Box>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', alignItems: 'center', marginTop: 10 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8B97A8' }}>DSC5001 · Statistical Machine Learning I</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#1E4FA8', fontWeight: 'bold' }}>Team 32 · 9/10</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
